WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.408
- It is such an honor to have you here.

00:00:02.408 --> 00:00:03.510
- My pleasure.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.010
- Oh my god, I'm so stoked.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.140
I was like, wait, what? Who's coming?

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.300
Like, it's the coolest
thing ever, to be a singer

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.830
and have this talk show, you
never thought you'd have.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.110
And then get to meet all
these heroes that, you know,

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.120
I've been listening to,
still listen to, oh my gosh.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.370
So, I'm gonna start with this,

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.350
Doja Cat, who I love,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.947
just sampled, was it Walk On By?

00:00:20.947 --> 00:00:21.780
- Walk On By.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.613
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:22.613 --> 00:00:23.446
Is that so cool?

00:00:23.446 --> 00:00:24.450
You're like listening to the songs,

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.770
like, coming right back around.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.940
- Yeah, it's amazing.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.770
I didn't know that it
had been recorded by her

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.490
and my granddaughter called...

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.323
- Wait, they don't have to...

00:00:33.323 --> 00:00:34.860
they have to ask
permission for that, right?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.532
- No, not really.

00:00:36.532 --> 00:00:39.120
(people laughing)

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.411
- That's a whole separate episode, okay.

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:43.860
- Yeah, they sample it, and it's theirs.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.693
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:00:44.693 --> 00:00:47.004
- But anyway, my granddaughter called me.

00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:47.837
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:49.605
- And asked, Grammy, I say yeah,

00:00:49.605 --> 00:00:52.683
do you know you're on
a record with Doja Cat?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.252
I said, Doja who?

00:00:55.252 --> 00:00:57.440
(people laughing)

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.240
She said, she's a rapper and she's a...

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.440
and she went into explaining
all of this to me.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.640
And I said, okay, and what
song are we talking about?

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.470
She said, Walk On By,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.873
completely through the entire song.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.630
Okay.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.880
Well apparently it's a major hit for her.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.091
- Oh, no, no, it's huge,
Paint The Town Red, yeah.

00:01:17.091 --> 00:01:18.060
(people laughing)

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.737
It's a solid hit that.

00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:21.210
- I'm thrilled for that, and like I said,

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.580
when I heard that it had been done,

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.530
I hope Walk On By is as good for her

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.970
as it has been for me.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.027
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:28.027 --> 00:01:28.860
- It's wonderful.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.150
- I think what's cool about
it too is like people...

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.482
I'm sorry, you can clap, you
were clapping, I'm sorry.

00:01:32.482 --> 00:01:35.385
(audience clapping)

00:01:35.385 --> 00:01:37.320
I think what's interesting
too, is, you know,

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.310
I grew up on that song.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.390
I love a lot of Burt Bacharach,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.340
obviously, a partner of yours,
that you worked with a lot.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.200
But, I just think it's cool

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.060
because you introduce people like a whole

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.170
different generation.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.003
- Yeah.

00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:48.180
- To songs that they might not have known.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.680
- Absolutely. And they're great songs.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:54.099
And finally they're being
exposed to, good music.

00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:54.997
Thank Jesus.

00:01:54.997 --> 00:01:56.088
- Yeah, Amen, yes, yes.

00:01:56.088 --> 00:01:57.256
(audience clapping)

00:01:57.256 --> 00:01:58.850
So, I have to ask, I didn't know this,

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.350
but, you're kind of, the
breakout moment for you

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.820
in your career was, it was the first night

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.080
that you were at Apollo, right?

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.220
- Yeah, we did, I did
the, it was a Gospel Show

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.380
and my group, The Gospelaires,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.213
up here on amateur night.

00:02:13.315 --> 00:02:17.820
And, it was really
weird, because we decided

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.310
to sing a song called It Goes That Wait.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.440
It was recorded by a
group out of Philadelphia.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.000
The Imperials.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.910
And we were appearing on the Gospel Show,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.820
and we had no idea that they were standing

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.100
in the wings while we sang their song.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.720
- Oh, were you happy, you didn't know?

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.300
- Yes, quite happy, believe me.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.793
But, they were so kind to us.

00:02:37.793 --> 00:02:40.980
You did a wonderful job,
we're thrilled about you

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.630
singing our song,

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.280
and as it turned out, we won.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.570
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.462
Well, people knew then,

00:02:47.462 --> 00:02:51.870
but I think what's even cooler
is I heard afterwards you,

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.220
they were like, hey, we're looking

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.990
for some singers to be on this record.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.580
And then you ended up in
the studio right after that.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:57.720
- Yep, sure did.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.423
Our group went to New York, New Jersey.

00:03:02.292 --> 00:03:03.125
The A Team.

00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:05.150
(people laughing)

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.390
at the Boy Records,

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.590
and we did our very
first background session.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.423
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:13.140
- For Sam "The Man" Taylor

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.640
and Nappy Brown.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.473
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:03:15.473 --> 00:03:17.439
- And that was our introduction to singing

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:19.350
the 'oohs' and 'ahs'
and the "yeah, yeah's"

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:20.790
that you hear on the recordings.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.220
- Yeah, I just think it's
a lesson too, to say Yes.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.840
because you were like, you
didn't even, you all...

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:25.890
I heard that you didn't even know what

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.300
you all were saying yes to, really.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.729
- Yeah, we didn't even
know what a background was.

00:03:29.729 --> 00:03:30.562
(people laughing)

00:03:30.562 --> 00:03:32.160
- You're just like, we'll do it.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.330
I love that, because you never

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.620
know what experience will come from that.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.720
You also had to, this,
I find this incredible

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.000
because it just seems so long ago,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.740
but it's actually not that long ago.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.480
But you toured during segregation.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.540
- Like, how incredibly difficult was that?

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.130
- It was interesting, to put it mildly.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.350
Something I'd never experienced before.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.183
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:53.183 --> 00:03:55.290
- But it was a case of, it was,

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.390
it became an adventure for me.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:01.920
I'm one of those real
rebels, real ones, that's me.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:02.753
- Yeah.

00:04:02.753 --> 00:04:06.240
- And, I had never experienced
anything that said,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.580
oh, you can't sit here
or you can't go there,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.040
or you can't drink this, or you can't...

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.330
- Can't sing this song.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.310
- Excuse me...

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:15.690
What you mean I can't?

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:19.050
No, of course, that doesn't
exist in my vocabulary.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.090
- Yeah, it's almost like when
they tell you that, it's like,

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.380
well, you've now made it a red button

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.213
that I will be pressing.

00:04:23.213 --> 00:04:24.046
- Will be pressing.

00:04:24.046 --> 00:04:24.879
- Yeah.

00:04:24.879 --> 00:04:25.712
- Several times.

00:04:25.712 --> 00:04:28.650
- Yeah, I heard that one
time that you, the club

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:29.850
or somewhere, where you
were performing said

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.350
they didn't want you to
perform a certain song

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.240
and you're like, that's in
my set, I'm going to sing it.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.680
And then you all had to get off the stage.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:35.513
They ended up...

00:04:35.513 --> 00:04:37.260
- Yeah, they closed the Show down.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.500
It was Ray Charles, What'd I Say,

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:45.157
and there's a verse in there
that I changed a little of.

00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:48.750
"tell your mama, tell
you Pa and I'm gonna..."

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.480
the words is "I'm gonna
send you back to Arkansas"

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.340
But I said, I'm gonna segregate,

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.320
I'm gonna integrate Arkansas.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.120
And they said, oh, you can't say that.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:57.953
Yes, I can.

00:04:57.953 --> 00:04:59.131
- [Kelly] Watch me.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:00.268
(people laughing)

00:05:00.268 --> 00:05:01.510
- I can, and I did.

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.343
- I love that.

00:05:02.343 --> 00:05:04.047
- And they shut the Show down

00:05:04.047 --> 00:05:05.122
(audience clapping)

00:05:05.122 --> 00:05:07.396
- It's important

00:05:07.396 --> 00:05:10.440
- So, I found this information out

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.480
and I was certain in my soul

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.400
that you had already been honored

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.510
at the Kennedy Center Honors.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.730
It's like in my mind when
I heard that, oh my gosh,

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.050
you're gonna be honored at
the Kennedy Center Honors.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.910
I was like, that hadn't already happened.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:24.000
Like, for me in my brain
that had already existed.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.006
- You and so many others, they thought

00:05:26.006 --> 00:05:27.480
I had already been honored.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:30.030
As a matter of fact,
even the Kennedy Honors

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.085
thought I had been honored.

00:05:31.085 --> 00:05:31.918
(audience laughing)

00:05:31.918 --> 00:05:33.720
- I know, I, whenever
it happened, I was like,

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.860
this has not happened yet.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.360
What's wrong with us, as a race.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:38.190
I don't understand the
human race right now.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.230
But I mean, you've worked
with, first of all,

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.648
congratulations on that.

00:05:41.648 --> 00:05:42.488
(audience cheering)

00:05:42.488 --> 00:05:43.748
That's incredible.

00:05:43.748 --> 00:05:46.040
I think it's over due, but
I think it's incredible.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:46.949
- Yes it is.

00:05:46.949 --> 00:05:49.290
- Yeah, well you have worked with

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.450
and influenced so many
artists in your career,

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.740
so we wanted to talk about a few.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.210
because there's so many amazing ones.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.430
So we're gonna start with
Elvis, which I just find

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:57.960
so random and awesome.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:01.140
I heard a story that was
really cool about this man

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:03.030
with you, but I wanna make sure it's real.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.130
And it involved him
like signing some stuff.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:05.963
- Yeah.

00:06:05.963 --> 00:06:07.920
- That happened, it's
real, tell them, okay.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.410
- I was opening at the Sands Hotel

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.617
and he was opening at the,

00:06:11.617 --> 00:06:15.330
well, at the Continental at the time.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.630
And I went over to see my
Aunt Sissy, who was a part

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.950
of The Sweet Inspirations,

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.050
who were backing him up on the show.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:22.883
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:22.883 --> 00:06:27.120
- And, was introduced to him
and he was such a nice man.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.053
Oh, and he's so pretty.

00:06:29.053 --> 00:06:31.320
(audience laughing)

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.140
He really was, but he was so kind.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.670
And he says, oh, you're opening tonight.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:38.580
I said, yeah, he says, I
am too, I said, I know.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:42.960
He said, well, when you go
to your news record store,

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.224
you're gonna find a surprise from me.

00:06:45.224 --> 00:06:46.057
I'm going to give you a gift.

00:06:46.057 --> 00:06:46.953
I said, okay.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.240
And in every single one of my albums,

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.710
he has signed an autograph
photograph and stuck it inside.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:59.520
And he made the announcement
from the stage, his stage,

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.190
that if you buy a Dionne Warwick CD

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.890
or what they call CDs
now, it was an album.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:06.840
- An album, yeah.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.620
- If you buy one, you'll
find a surprise inside of it.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.170
And it was a photograph of him.

00:07:13.429 --> 00:07:15.763
- That is so cool.

00:07:15.763 --> 00:07:16.803
- Yeah.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.750
- I mean, just that an
artist goes out their way

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.310
to support another artist.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.143
- I know.

00:07:21.143 --> 00:07:23.130
- That's incredible, there's
so many cool things about that.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.504
I bet sales were well.

00:07:24.504 --> 00:07:26.606
(audience laughing)

00:07:26.606 --> 00:07:27.439
- You tell me.

00:07:27.439 --> 00:07:30.630
- I was like, I bet they ran.
They were like, and later.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.550
Okay, so I heard this story too,

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.660
which I just,

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.280
you are so gangster.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:38.970
So I heard that you
called, is it Snoop Dogg

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.860
and Suge Knight to your
house for a meeting?

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:41.693
- Yes.

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:43.456
- Please tell everyone the story,

00:07:43.456 --> 00:07:44.340
(audience laughing)

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.930
because you were listening to,

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.280
and this is probably the age they were

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.793
so wait, so you were listening
to a song with your son?

00:07:49.793 --> 00:07:50.760
- With my son.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:51.593
- Okay.

00:07:51.593 --> 00:07:53.940
- Yes, as it turns out,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:57.960
Damon, was in the car with me

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.813
and this rap thing came on.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.000
Ugh...

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.131
(audience laughing)

00:08:05.131 --> 00:08:07.680
And he was saying

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:10.167
every single word of it.

00:08:10.167 --> 00:08:12.180
And I turned the radio off and said,

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.800
how do you know every
single word of this song?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.693
He said, oh, that's rap.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.540
I said, yeah, okay.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.873
I said, do you know the
Declaration of Independence?

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.240
Ah, no.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.354
- Silent.

00:08:25.354 --> 00:08:26.187
(people laughing)

00:08:26.187 --> 00:08:28.200
- I said, well, I'll tell you what,

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.300
until you learn every single word of the

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.940
Declaration of Independence
and you say it to me

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.010
- Rehearse it, yeah.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.210
- You will not listen
to this kind of music.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.500
Oh mommy.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.113
Yeah, oh mommy is right.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.080
- But then you called them to your house.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.480
- Yeah, I called them to
the house based on the fact

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.763
that they were all using,

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.240
kind of not such nice words.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.193
- Yeah, especially towards women.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.800
- And you know, I kind of,

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.700
and I was one of the very
first ones to combat them

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.670
with what they were
saying, misogynistic words,

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.950
calling young ladies
out the name, you know.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.900
I said, how many young
ladies do you see walking

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.850
around on four legs with a tail,

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.737
you know, and calling them out the names.

00:09:13.737 --> 00:09:15.737
(audience laughing)

00:09:15.737 --> 00:09:20.724
(audience clapping)

00:09:20.724 --> 00:09:22.826
- I love it.

00:09:22.826 --> 00:09:27.810
- Yes well, I made it my
business to let them know that

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.180
you made me part of the problem.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:33.270
Now I want you to make
me part of the solution.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:34.103
- Yeah.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:35.963
I'll tell you what,

00:09:35.963 --> 00:09:38.967
I actually had the opportunity
to work with Snoop, as well,

00:09:38.967 --> 00:09:40.590
and you must have made an impact.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.850
because he's so respectful.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.530
